    {"id":"b3-web-kyber-sacred","record_kind":"external-claim","research_question":"What does official material establish about kyber crystals before Perun treats one as engineering material?","source_type":"web-official","source_title":"Kyber Crystal (Lightsaber Crystal) | Star Wars Databank","branch":"Canon","source_era":"era-invariant reference","locator":{"kind":"web","url":"https://www.starwars.com/databank/lightsaber-crystal","accessed_at":"2026-09-04"},"statement":"The official Databank places a kyber crystal at the heart of every Jedi lightsaber, says kyber crystals are found on several planets and describes a personal Force attunement between a specific crystal and a Jedi. Kyber crystals are therefore a class of objects rather than one unique relic; the individual bond and properties of a particular specimen may be distinctive.","confidence":"high","disposition":"adapted","adaptation_note":"Perun's difficulty is obtaining and using a suitable intact specimen without exposing himself, not the uniqueness of kyber crystals as a class. Project canon allows a specially processed kyber crystal to operate only as a non-native surrogate in the archaeotech droid. The native power energy crystals are a separate project-specific technology unrelated to kyber crystals or the Force. By direct author decision, first contact through the installed processed kyber teaches Perun's main multidimensional body to use the Force; the acquired ability persists without the crystal and can act through effector-controlled bodies. The droid brains do not become independently Force-sensitive, and ordinary network machines do not inherit this ability. The artifact is Perun's former armor, a closed author truth; its native personal-computation expansion requires native crystals and is not activated by the surrogate. These mechanisms are project adaptations, not claims established by the external source.","era_dependency":"era-invariant","target_time_window":{"start_years_before_birth":70,"end_years_before_birth":40},"comparison_category":"not-applicable","comparison_status":"same","target_era_evidence":["b3-web-kyber-sacred"],"relevance_tags":["kyber-crystal","lightsaber","jedi","surrogate","power-energy-crystal"],"narrative_uses":[{"function":"wonder","goal":"separate the processed kyber-crystal surrogate from the archaeotech droid's native power energy crystals","location":"archaeotech droid and auction trail","pov":"Perun","use_statement":"Ground the kyber crystal in Star Wars canon, mark its processed use as a surrogate, and never transfer its Force properties to the native power energy crystals."}],"conflicts":["The surrogate application of a processed kyber crystal has no external proof and is project-specific.","The native Heart, Mirror and Beacon power energy crystals are not kyber crystals and have no relation to the Force."]},
